00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:03.204
Did you know that there is a global
experiment performed

00:00:03.204 --> 00:00:06.496
on approximately 1.6 billion people

00:00:06.496 --> 00:00:09.496
across 75 countries twice a year?

00:00:09.663 --> 00:00:12.454
It’s called daylight saving time.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.454
[Sleeping with Science]

00:00:17.496 --> 00:00:22.579
The sleep-associated consequences
are more significant than you may realize.

00:00:22.704 --> 00:00:24.329
For example in the spring,

00:00:24.329 --> 00:00:26.246
when we lose one hour of sleep,

00:00:26.246 --> 00:00:31.413
there is a subsequent 24 percent
relative increase in heart attacks.

00:00:31.621 --> 00:00:33.329
In contrast, in the fall --

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:34.329
in the autumn,

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:36.454
when we gain an hour of sleep,

00:00:36.454 --> 00:00:40.371
there is a 21 percent reduction
in heart attacks.

00:00:40.746 --> 00:00:42.246
Isn’t that incredible?

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:43.662
And I should also note

00:00:43.662 --> 00:00:48.537
that we see similar changes
in things such as road traffic accidents,

00:00:48.537 --> 00:00:49.621
strokes

00:00:49.621 --> 00:00:52.662
and, tragically, suicide rates as well.

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:55.537
In fact, even the economy suffers

00:00:55.537 --> 00:00:59.162
with certain stock market returns
taking a downswing

00:00:59.162 --> 00:01:01.787
following the shift
to daylight saving time

00:01:01.787 --> 00:01:03.829
and that one hour of lost sleep.

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:07.329
This is how fragile our brains,

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:08.496
our bodies

00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:10.538
and even our societies are

00:01:10.538 --> 00:01:11.913
when it comes to sleep loss.

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:14.121
But said more positively,

00:01:14.121 --> 00:01:17.121
even just small increases in sleep

00:01:17.121 --> 00:01:20.954
can have immediate
as well as long-term health benefits.

00:01:21.121 --> 00:01:24.871
So rather than thinking
of sleep as a cost,

00:01:24.871 --> 00:01:26.746
we can instead think of sleep

00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:30.038
as one of the very best
investments we can make.

